        <activityName xml:lang="en">Eucalyptus ssp., standing, under bark, u=50%, in plantation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Eucalyptus ssp., standing, under bark, u=50%, in plantation
data refers to wood 'under bark'. CO2 assimilation is based on 49.4% carbon in the wood including the bark (10%). Biomass energy equals gross calorific value including bark.\nTechnology: natural growth;
Synonyms: Eucalyptus camaldulensis; 
UUID: 339cbd3f-5f30-3790-8654-455ed5efe331
includes the CO2 absorption from air and the land use for the trees to grow (including 15% bark). Forest road area is not included in the land use. Density: 825 kg/m3 (u=0)
Location: undefined
Technology: natural growth; relates to the forest area and CO2 from air needed to produce eucalyptus
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_339cbd3f-5f30-3790-8654-455ed5efe331.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
